    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.alphalete.icd-onboarding-seed-names</string>

    <!-- STEP 7 ONLY: put this week's new starts on the OBCL, three times an
         hour. Megan 2026-11-22: a name BOB'd at 2:05 should be on the
         extension at 2:15, not at 2:30.

         :05, :20 and :50 — OFF THE BOARD'S MINUTES, which are :00, :15, :30
         and :45. This used to run at :00/:15/:45, avoiding only :30 because
         the hourly board run fired at half past. The board moved to the hour
         (9f7a7bd5) and that avoidance stopped avoiding anything: the two
         then collided at nearly every fire, and since they refuse to run
         beside each other the overlap guard was skipping one of them. The
         collision test could not see it because this pair of plists was not
         well-formed XML and the parser gave up before reading a single time.
         Megan, 2026-11-25, on why it matters now: "it's going to run on ECO
         machines" — one skipped sweep on a Lucy is a late name; on forty
         office machines it is forty. The other eight columns stay on the hourly
         com.alphalete.icd-onboarding run: they are a browser walk through
         OwnerVille, Blue Ink and the Sterling inbox, and four of those an hour
         buys nothing. SENDS NOTHING.
         Install: lucy rerun install_icd_onboarding_seed_names_agent machine "<Lucy N>" -->

    <!-- Path is the laptop placeholder; install_agent.py rewrites it to the
         target machine's repo path. -->
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder/deploy/icd_onboarding_seed_names.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PYTHONPATH</key>
        <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder</string>
    </dict>

    <!-- :00, :15 and :45 from 6am to 8pm, machine-local, every day.

         NOT :30. The hourly board run fires at half past and seeds as its
         first step, so a seed there would be the same work twice, racing
         itself for the same AppStream session. The hourly run IS the :30 pass,
         which is why this is three fires an hour and not four.

         Every day including Sunday, same reason the hourly run is: the week is
         seeded off the training calendar, and somebody brought on board at the
         weekend should not wait for Monday to appear. -->
